-# IceBarrageTimer
+# Ice Barrage Timer
 
-[![Buy Me a Coffee](https://img.shields.io/badge/Buy%20Me%20a%20Coffee-%E2%82%AC%F0%9F%9F%BD?style=for-the-badge)](https://ko-fi.com/affanfareed)
-
-## Overview
-A standalone OSRS plugin that tracks Ice Barrage and Teleblock timers on players you've attacked. Designed to work with RuneLite's latest client versions.
+Ice Barrage Timer is a RuneLite external plugin for PvP practice and fights. It watches your local game chat for successful Ice Barrage and Teleblock casts, starts a timer for the target player, and shows active timers in a compact overlay.
 
 ## Features
-- Player freezing notifications
-- Timer overlay showing remaining freeze duration
-- Teleblock tracking
 
-## Installation
-1. Download the latest `.jar` file from the releases section
-2. Place the JAR file in your `~/.runelite/plugins/` directory
-3. Enable the plugin in the RuneLite plugin menu
+- Tracks successful `Your Ice Barrage hits ... for ...` messages and starts a configurable freeze timer.
+- Tracks successful `Your Teleblock hits ... for ...` messages and starts a configurable teleblock timer.
+- Overlay lists active frozen and teleblocked players with remaining seconds.
+- Optional desktop notification when a timer starts.
+- Automatically expires timers on game ticks.
 
-## Usage
-After using Ice Barrage or Teleblock, timers automatically appear for targeted players.
+## Configuration
 
-## Contributing
-Pull requests are welcome! Please read our [Contributing Guidelines](CONTRIBUTING.md) first.
+The RuneLite config group is `icebarragetimer`.
 
----
+| Setting | Default | Description |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| Show overlay | On | Adds/removes the active timer overlay. |
+| Ice Barrage duration | 20 seconds | Freeze duration used for cleanup and overlay countdowns. |
+| Teleblock duration | 300 seconds | Teleblock duration used for cleanup and overlay countdowns. |
+| Notifications | Off | Sends a RuneLite notification when a timer starts. |
 
-*Created with ❤️ by Affan Fareed (Cloud Engineer, GM Financial)*
+## Development setup
+
+This repo follows the standard independent RuneLite external-plugin layout:
+
+- `runelite-plugin.properties` points RuneLite/plugin-hub at `com.itmeansbigmountain.icebarragetimer.IceBarrageTimerPlugin`.
+- `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/icebarragetimer/` contains the plugin, config, and overlay.
+- `src/test/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/icebarragetimer/` contains lightweight JVM tests and the developer-mode launcher.
+
+Use Java 11 when building locally:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+To run a local RuneLite client in developer mode from this checkout:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+./gradlew run --no-daemon
+```
+
+## Manual RuneLite testing checklist
+
+Before plugin-hub submission, verify in a live RuneLite session:
+
+1. Plugin appears as `Ice Barrage Timer` and can be enabled/disabled.
+2. The overlay appears when `Show overlay` is enabled and disappears when disabled.
+3. A successful Ice Barrage chat line starts a freeze timer for the correct target name.
+4. A successful Teleblock chat line starts a teleblock timer for the correct target name.
+5. Custom duration settings affect both overlay countdowns and timer expiry.
+6. Optional notifications trigger only when `Notifications` is enabled.
+
+## API usage
+
+This plugin does not call external APIs. It only consumes RuneLite client events (`ChatMessage`, `GameTick`, and config changes) and uses RuneLite overlay/notification services.
